## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design an end-to-end data governance workflow with real-time drift detection across tenants, leveraging Data Catalog tagging, BigQuery taxonomy, and alerting. Focuses on correctness, security, and scalability trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Data taxonomy in BigQuery and how to surface it for tagging
- Data Catalog tagging API for dynamic resource labeling
- Drift detection patterns in streaming pipelines
- Idempotent processing guarantees in Dataflow and BigQuery inserts
- Observability and alert routing to Cloud Run/Slack and BigQuery summaries

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: apply a Data Catalog tag to a resource
const {DataCatalogClient} = require('@google-cloud/datacatalog');
const client = new DataCatalogClient();
async function tagResource(resourceName, tagTemplate, fields) {
  const [tag] = await client.createTag({
    parent: resourceName,
    tag: {
      template: tagTemplate,
      fields: fields
    }
  });
  return tag;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle taxonomy evolution without breaking existing tags?
- What metrics would you monitor to balance false positives vs drift detection latency?

